  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "A proton and an <math><mi>&#945;</mi></math>- particle (with their masses in the ratio of <math><mn>1</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>4</mn></math> and charges in the ratio of <math><mn>1</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>2</mn></math> ) are accelerated from rest through a potential difference <math><mi>V</mi><mo>.</mo></math> If a uniform magnetic field <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is set up perpendicular to their velocities, the ratio of the radii <math><msub><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:</mo><msub><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi></mrow></msub></math> of the circular paths described by them will be:",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "d4nGL",
      "text": "<math><mn>1</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>3</mn></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "5fANC",
      "text": "<math><mn>1</mn><mo>:</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></math>",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Kwlkh",
      "text": "<math><mn>1</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>2</mn></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "8ep1n",
      "text": "<math><mn>1</mn><mo>:</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The kinetic energy of a charge&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>q</mi></math>&nbsp;of mass&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math>&nbsp;in potential is given by,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>q</mi><mi>V</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi><mi>q</mi><mi>V</mi></msqrt></math></p><p>Then, the radius of the charge will be,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msqrt><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi><mi>q</mi><mi>V</mi></msqrt><mrow><mi>q</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>&#8733;</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mi>m</mi><mi>q</mi></mfrac></msqrt></math></p><p>Hence, the ratio of radius of proton to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi></math>-particle,<br /><br /><math><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo></math><math><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></math>.</p></blockquote>",
